cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NORMA or its CPAD engine, please cite it."
title: "NORMA: learn the denial constraints governing a table, detect errors, and normalize it"
abstract: >-
  NORMA discovers the functional dependencies and denial constraints a relational table
  satisfies, scores per-cell data-quality errors by their degree of violation (the CPAD
  engine), and derives a 3NF/BCNF normalized schema. It exports the discovered constraints
  to the data-quality ecosystem (Great Expectations, pandera, dbt, SQL, JSON Schema,
  Frictionless, Metanome, SHACL).
type: software
# TODO(release): replace the placeholder author(s) with the real names + ORCIDs before
# the public, post-acceptance release. Kept anonymous here for double-blind review.
authors:
  - name: "NORMA contributors"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/normaCPAD/norma"
keywords:
  - data quality
  - denial constraints
  - functional dependencies
  - error detection
  - database normalization
  - anomaly detection
version: 0.1.0
